{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/148062-fun-thought-experiment-more-bloodlines-from-traditions","id":148062,"title":"Fun Thought Experiment: More Bloodlines from Traditions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-24T12:57:55-07:00","id":148062,"title":"Fun Thought Experiment: More Bloodlines from Traditions?","content":"So Vampire has one clan and one bloodline that both exist as the result of Mages doing some experiments with themselves; the Tremere began as a House of the Order of Hermes and the Nagaraja are a splinter of the Chakravanti (now Euthanatoi). As a fun idea, let's consider what the remaining Traditions might make of becoming Kindred?<br /> <br /> The Verbena strike me as the most likely, due to their superficial tie to blood magic, but I'm struggling to see them as anything more than a combination of Gangrel and Lamia. I don't want to imagine how absurd Virtual Adept vampires would be, but I'm desperate to see what the Sons of Ether might do with the Kindred condition. There's also the Akashics, Celestial Chorus, Dreamspeakers, Cult of Ecstasy, and the Conventions of the Technocracy. (Vat-grown Vampires with heavy mental programming? Sign me up for a dozen).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T14:18:48-07:00","id":148116,"title":"","content":"We already have the Verbena Bloodline - the Lhiannan. It would have been neat to see more done with th